-- title:
--   Transport of pole-chart regularity along an automorphism fixing j
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, where $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the image of that rational function field under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((t))$ the base change along [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= t^{-1}\cdot$(the $j$-numerator power series over $\mathbb{Q}$). Write $B =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Fix $\varpi \in A$ and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with $\sigma(j) = j$. Let $Y$ be a prime ideal of $B$ such that every localisation $C_{\mathfrak m}$ of $B$ at $Y$ is a regular local ring and $C_{\mathfrak m}/(\varpi)$ is a regular local ring, and let $Y'$ be a prime ideal of $B$ whose elements are exactly the $\sigma(b)$ for $b \in Y$. Then for every localisation $B_{\mathfrak m}$ of $B$ at $Y'$, both $B_{\mathfrak m}$ and $B_{\mathfrak m}/(\varpi)$ are regular local rings.
--
--   This is a transport-of-structure step in the study of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: regularity of the local ring at a point of the chart around $j = \infty$, together with regularity of its fibre over a uniformiser, propagates from a prime $Y$ to any Galois translate $\sigma(Y)$ under an $L$-automorphism of the function field fixing $j$. It feeds the statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three), where regularity proved at one prime of the pole chart is spread over its orbit.
